    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower at the top of the order, headlined by **Kyle Schwarber** (73.66) and **Trea Turner** (72.84). Both benefit from an advantageous matchup against Kikuchi and favorable wind conditions, providing a high-ceiling foundation for our 5x5 run production. **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** also commands attention with a 69.90 score; despite a marginal SP matchup against Springs, he benefits from a +10% park factor adjustment that elevates his power profile into elite territory for today\u2019s utility slot. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains a high-upside play at 69.09, though his status hinges on a \"Lineup Pending\" tag; if he secures the leadoff spot against Burns, his speed profile provides the necessary boost to our scarcest category, SB.\n\nThe decision-making process for the bottom of the order was dictated by a strict adherence to our 40.0 efficiency floor. **Hector Rodriguez** was the most difficult exclusion, finishing at 47.44; however, with a difficult matchup against Imanaga and a suboptimal platoon situation, he fell behind the more favorable pairings for **Christian Yelich** and **Yordan Alvarez**. **Dillon Dingler** also faced a difficult path, landing at 35.06\u2014well below our threshold\u2014due to the daunting prospect of facing Glasnow. We are prioritizing the higher-probability matchups for **Junior Caminero** and **Carson Benge** today, both of whom carry significant SP skill-based advantages (19%) that outweigh the potential output of our bench depth. While **Gary Sanchez** and **Kazuma Okamoto** anchor the middle of the order with scores hovering near the 45\u201350 range, they provide the necessary stability to bridge the gap between our high-scoring anchors and our fringe-roster utility plays.",
